+# Forward-GRACE ("prod") extension:
+# In addition to the original full-model projected gradients, this script can
+# compute a forward-only feature per example: the exact output-readout gradient
+# term G = (1/n_sup) * R^T H, where R stacks r_t = softmax(logits_t) - onehot(label_t)
+# and H stacks the post-final-norm last hidden states h_t over supervised
+# (label != -100) shifted positions. Because HF's causal-LM loss is mean-CE over
+# supervised tokens, G is exactly the derivative through the output-readout use
+# of lm_head.weight (verified by scripts/sanity_prod_gate.py). For an untied
+# lm_head this is the parameter-block gradient. If input/output weights are tied,
+# the total shared-parameter gradient also contains the input-embedding path.
+# Two projected variants are produced:
+#   PRIMARY  ("prod"):    flatten G (V*d dims, row-major over V) through a
+#                         CudaProjector(grad_dim=V*d, proj_dim=args.proj_dim,
+#                         seed=0, rademacher), divided by sqrt(V*d) — mirroring
+#                         the full-grad convention (divide by sqrt(grad_dim)).
+#   SECONDARY ("prod2s"): two-sided Rademacher sketch S_r: V->32, S_h: d->16
+#                         (both drawn from a CPU torch.Generator with seed 0,
+#                         S_r first then S_h), computed tokenwise as
+#                         (R S_r)^T (H S_h) / n_sup without materializing G,
+#                         flattened to 512 dims and divided by sqrt(V*d) for
+#                         convention-consistency with the primary variant.
+# Row order of all output pickles is identical (the per-example dataset order),
+# so GRACE_computation.py consumes any of them unchanged.
+#
+# GRACE paper compatibility:
+#   --row-scale grace_log_length multiplies every stored row (full, prod, and
+#   prod2s) by log(n_sup), where n_sup is the shifted supervised-token count used
+#   by HF's mean-CE denominator. The default 'none' preserves released behavior.
+#
+# Projection reproducibility (opt-in):
+#   trak's CudaProjector passes the GPU's streaming-multiprocessor count to
+#   fast_jl, and the Rademacher sign stream depends on it, so the same seed gives
+#   a different projection on a GPU with a different SM count. The stored LESSER
+#   paper features used num_sms=128 (the RTX 4090 value). --num-sms pins the
+#   value for every projector; the default (None) keeps the GPU's own count,
+#   which is the released behavior.
+#
+# Memory protocol (keeps fp32 computation exactly; fits 24GB GPUs):
+#   - 'both' mode runs TWO passes per example: (a) a torch.no_grad() forward for
+#     the prod features, with aggressive del + empty_cache, then (b) the ORIGINAL
+#     unmodified forward + loss.backward() full-gradient path. The fp32 (T, V)
+#     logits held for backward therefore never coexist with the prod workspace,
+#     capping peak memory at plain-GRACE level at the cost of one extra forward.
+#   - The prod softmax / R^T H accumulation is chunked over the time dimension
+#     (<= PROD_CHUNK_TOKENS supervised tokens per chunk) so a second full (T, V)
+#     fp32 tensor is never materialized alongside the model's own logits.
+#   - INTENTIONAL DIVERGENCE from the upstream path: for examples longer
+#     than FULL_GRAD_CKPT_THRESHOLD_TOKENS, the full-gradient pass enables HF
+#     gradient checkpointing (use_reentrant=False) for that example only. The
+#     plain fp32 forward+backward itself OOMs on 24GB at T>~42xx (a T=5668
+#     example allocates >23.6GiB in the FORWARD), and the
+#     GSM8K synthetic sets contain 1-8 such examples per teacher (max T=5668).
+#     Checkpointing replays the same fp32 ops during backward; the gradient is
+#     fp32-machine-precision equivalent, not bitwise (recompute may select
+#     different fp32 kernels): measured rel L2 diff ~5e-6 on the projected row,
+#     checked against tol 1e-4, 10x tighter than the 1e-3 tolerance of scripts/sanity_prod_gate.py
+#     (see check_ckpt_equivalence in scripts/memory_probe_both.py). Dropout must
+#     be zero for the temporary .train() flip to be a no-op; asserted below.
